Most populous city (municipal) | **Lucknow**, not Kanpur
@end

@up UP link: UP's density (**829**) is over twice the national figure, and **Ghaziabad** (3,971) and **Varanasi** are its densest districts, with **Lalitpur** the sparsest. Literacy rose from 56.3% (2001) to 67.7% (2011), but the **20-point gender gap** remains one of India's widest.

@trap
**India's density 382 (2011); rose every census.** **Bihar densest, Arunachal sparsest; Delhi densest UT, Andaman sparsest.** **Literacy counted from age 7.** **India 74.04% (M 82.14, F 65.46; gap 16.68).** **Kerala > Mizoram.** **Bihar lowest; Lakshadweep top UT.** **Biggest literacy jump 1991-2001.** **Meghalaya smallest gender gap.** **UP 67.7%; best G.B. Nagar, worst Shravasti.** **Jaunpur highest UP sex ratio; Lalitpur lowest density.**
@end

